  "notes": "T_XY = substitution of the atoms along the word XY, with Tr(T_XY) = T_YX by (S[T])^d = S^d[T^d] and X^d = Y. Writing a(w) = log2|E(T_w)|, composition gives a(w) + a(wbar) = 3(2^k - 1) for every word of length k, so the family's threshold ratio max(a, abar)/(2^k - 1) is at least 3/2, and a(w) - a(wbar) is odd so it is never met. The constant words XX..X and YY..Y are exactly the GK- and TK-families and are the worst-balanced ones, both at 2; this mixed word sits at 5/3, strictly past the tight families of Observation 2.3.3.",
